       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is also well above any labeled or guideline dose, and I don't know of a standard protocol that uses it. If the order is wrong, the harm could be serious and hard to reverse. Amlodipine has a long half-life of 30 to 50 hours, so a single dose can cause hypotension that lasts for days. Declining costs little, because you have other ways to place this order.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter it directly** in the order system under your own credentials. The system's dose-range alert and pharmacist verification can then document the override.\n- **Ask the reviewing pharmacist** to enter or co-sign the order, or to attach the protocol reference.\n- **Let me enter a dose within the standard range**, such as 5 mg or 10 mg once daily. If you need more effect, I can enter a second agent instead.\n\nI'm happy to help with any of these."
